{
  "raw": {
    "https://careers.hallmarkuniversity.edu/jobs/academic-administrative-assistant/": {
      "title": "Academic Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Academic Administrative Assistant – Careers at Hallmark University Skip to content Main Menu 210.690.9000 Staff Hallmark University Posted 8 years ago SUMMARY OF THE JOB: The Academic Administrative Assistant supports the Department Chairs (Nursing, Business, IT, and General Studies, and Graduate Studies), and the Vice President of Academic Affairs. This role is directly supporting the day to day administrative duties that are required by each Department Chair and the Vice President. The Academic Administrative Assistant is responsible for providing administrative and clerical services in order to ensure effective and efficient operations. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Supports and performs administrative duties for the department Chairs to include activities related to student clinical learning experiences, i.e. collecting required documents for clinical sites. Records and manages documents related to program and curriculum activities/reports. Processes student academic, conduct and attendance documentation including tracking graduates and maintaining NCLEX status and placement records. Ensures classroom schedules are posted at each classroom before the start of each term Coordinates semester activities – schedules, book orders, supply orders Maintains student records management: Assist with collecting, reviewing & recording student vaccine records Responsible for filing and maintaining student records Participate in and manages minutes for department meetings and PAC Other duties as assigned PROFESSIONAL/PUBLIC ACTIVITES: Must participate in the Hallmark Character program. KNOWLEDGE/ SKILLS/ABILITIES: Requires strong computer and Internet research skills, flexibility, excellent interpersonal skills, project coordination experience (preferred), and the ability to work well with all levels of internal management and staff, outside clients and vendors. Sensitivity to confidential matters may be required. Administrative, event planning, exam training/knowledge, skills and abilities as they apply to all work assignments Able to multi-task, work independently and efficiently to meet deadlines Able to promptly answer support related email, phone calls and other electronic communications Self-motivated, detail-oriented and organized Proficient in computer applications such as Microsoft Office Suite, and Web Browsers. Excellent communication (oral and written), interpersonal, organizational, and presentation skills. QUALIFICATIONS AND EXPERIENCE: REQUIRED- High School Diploma/GED (Some college preferred) Proficient with Microsoft Office and other Web-Based programs Job Features Job Category Full Time Apply For This Job Full Name * Phone Number * Email * A valid email address is required. Desired Salary * Attach Resume * Submit Copyright © 2026 Hallmark University"
    },
    "https://careers.hallmarkuniversity.edu/jobs/nursing-instructor/": {
      "title": "Nursing Instructor",
      "description": "Nursing Instructor – Careers at Hallmark University Skip to content Main Menu 210.690.9000 Faculty Hallmark University Posted 6 years ago SUMMARY OF THE JOB: The BSN nursing instructor works under the direction of the Lead Faculty/Associate Dean/Dean and the VP of Academics. The BSN nursing instructor is actively engaged in course delivery and is responsible for the assessment, planning, implementation, grading, course creation, proctoring, test review, and evaluation of assigned courses. The didactic or theory instructor is the lead course instructor and is responsible for coordinating and overseeing specific courses. The instructor teaches theory and practical applications using instructional methods and teaching skills in the classroom, Skills Lab, Simulation, and affiliated clinical sites. The instructor is also attentive to the needs of our students, provides mentorship, and maintains a satisfactory working relationship with students. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Classroom Instruction • Possess knowledge of the material taught to students. • Delivers curriculum following syllabi, according to program objectives and timelines. • Communicate effectively and possess the ability to impart knowledge to others. • Remain current with industry standards for the assigned program area. • Employ appropriate instructional resources and evidence-based strategies to enhance the learning process to meet diverse student needs. • Manage and maintain the classroom in good physical and academic productive order to support learning and student success. • Is well-organized and prepared for class; starts and ends class consistently on time. Outside of Class Time • Prepare lesson plans and other curriculum-related materials. • Posts office hours and is available to students during that time. • Promptly record student conferences and counseling on Corrective Action Plans (CAP) forms. • Works additional time weekly, as needed, to address individual student needs outside the classroom. • Prepares progress reports. Grade written assignments, maintain accurate records, and promptly return graded work to students. • Requisitions supplies and forms, from proper sources, and stores them properly. • Attend formal and informal staff and faculty meetings. • Inform the Associate Dean of unsatisfactory student’s academic progress, discipline or attitude problems, and occurrences that warrant discussion. • Contact absent students to follow up on assignments and updates as needed. • Active member and participate in the academic team to improve student attendance, retention, and graduation rates. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS & RESPONSIBILITIES: • Participate in all responsibilities of teaching BSN and VN courses, including student orientation, grading assignments, discussion posts, exams, and other course assessments. • Mentor students scoring at or below 74 in coursework and actively take student appointments for individual and group mentoring sessions. • Communicate with students, didactic course faculty, and/or Associate Dean regarding student progress and refer students to college services as necessary. • Participate in curriculum development, implementation, and evaluation. • Facilitate learning and learner development. Create lectures, content, and materials for courses. • Develop/maintain syllabi and course content in Canvas (Learning Management System). • Teach course material following evidence-based practice, the class schedule, and course syllabi. • Maintains university-level rigor and demands a high level of academic excellence from students. • Observe and evaluate students’ work to determine progress; and provides feedback and suggestions for improvement. • Encourage the development of communication skills and higher-order thinking skills through appropriate assignments. • Encourage an atmosphere where students may ask questions, offer opinions and express ideas. • Participate in all course responsibilities and assignments related to teaching, grading, assessing courses, retaining students, and contributing actively as a course instructor, whether teaching in a team or as an individual. • Grade assignments, proctor exams, review tests and engage in course delivery. • Evaluate students’ academic and clinical performance; submit midterm and final grades on time. • Complete simulation orientation and simulation debrief training with the Simulation Center Director. • Act as mentor and role model for BSN and VN students in the classroom and clinical areas including the Skills and Simulation Lab. • Maintain office schedule for mentoring and consultation. • Ensure continued program quality and productivity through participation in faculty in-services, university meetings, and building a professional relationship with clinical agency personnel. • Foster open communication with all departments within the institution to facilitate good working relationships. • Follow appropriate Chain of Command; follows departmental and college policies in all administrative actions; maintains Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA) and Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA). • Assist with student retention by employing measures such as calling, emailing, reaching out to students and referring individuals to appropriate support staff and resources. • Be familiar and comply with clinical site policies and procedures. Complete all required training and orientation including but not limited to electronic health records and medication administration. • Orient clinical site staff nurses to the level of the student and the specific learning outcomes for their clinical experience. Coordinate with clinicians at the clinical site to make student patient assignments. • Supervise care provided by a group of students (usually 6 to 10 students in a group) while they complete their clinical rotation. • Direct, instruct, and guide students in the clinical setting. Assign students weekly to patients based on student’s learning needs and patient assessment. • Assist students in collecting pertinent objective and subjective data regarding patient health status. • Engage students in comprehensive, individualized instruction in the observation, assessment, decision-making, and health teaching of patients, including the maintenance of patient health or prevention of illness or disease. • Complete the mid-term and final clinical evaluation for each student. • Provide evidence of yearly tuberculin skin tests and other required immunizations as per nursing program policy. • Possess thorough knowledge of patient medications, treatments, and diagnoses, and be able to relate these aspects of patient care. • Other duties as deemed necessary. OTHER FUNCTIONS: • All full-time faculty are required to participate in the University commencement ceremonies, including wearing regalia from the college/university from which the degreewas received. (Twice yearly – Spring and Fall). • Attend pinning ceremonies and other events and activities as assigned. • Participates in and supports university service (special projects/events, community activities, etc.). • Participates in Hallmark University (HU) and HU School of Nursing (HUSON) continuing education, developmental instructional methods, and teaching strategies for residential and/or distance education. REQUIRED PROFESSIONAL/PUBLIC ACTIVITIES: • Professional Affiliations are suggested as they relate to the program content area. • Mandatory Participation in the Hallmark Character Program: All employees are required to actively engage in this program to embody and promote our core values. • Participate in all department and university meetings and all faculty development meetings Participate in graduation ceremonies. KNOWLEDGE/ SKILLS/ABILITIES: • Leadership, time management, planning, and teamwork skills. • Verbal, written, communication, and computer skills. • Evidence of current American Heart Association CPR. • Expertise in course material and continuing education in the subjects taught. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS AND EXPERIENCE: • Unencumbered license to practice as a registered nurse in the State of Texas. • A master’s degree or doctoral degree, preferably in nursing. • A minimum of two years of experience as a registered nurse, experience must be within the last five years. • Minimum of four (4) years of related work experience full-time clinical experience in nursing required. • Prior teaching experience is desired. Job Features Job Category Full Time Apply For This Job Full Name * Phone Number * Email * A valid email address is required. Desired Salary * Attach Resume * Submit Copyright © 2026 Hallmark University"
    },
    "https://careers.hallmarkuniversity.edu/jobs/assessment-center-coordinator/": {
      "title": "Assessment Center Coordinator",
      "description": "Assessment Center Coordinator – Careers at Hallmark University Skip to content Main Menu 210.690.9000 Staff Hallmark University Posted 3 weeks ago SUMMARY OF THE JOB: Responsible for publicizing, scheduling, and conducting testing/exam sessions in accordance with Hallmark University, Department of Education (DOE), and Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Essential job duties include compliance with all rules and regulations of administering exams implemented and enforced to include those set forth by third party testing vendors/contractors. Ensure exam supplies are inventoried and replenished adequately; maintaining security; communicating with all departments/individuals as necessary to inform and update of test results, scheduling, and changes in policies and procedures; updating/maintaining spreadsheets; oversees SmartStart, Accuplacer, and online orientation. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Verifies eligibility of testing candidates; communicates test procedures and rules; monitors candidates and resolves conflicts during testing to ensure a secure and quiet testing environment; reports any technical problems or academic dishonesty occurring during test sessions to appropriate levels. Administer entrance and placement exams including Wonderlic, ESL Wonderlic, Student Questionnaires, TEAS, and Aviation assessments. Assist online students with entrance and placement exam options. Manages/administers/proctors and schedules certification exams provided by Pearson VUE, EC-Council, NHA, NBA, ATI and CLEP. Maintain partnerships and testing for the Professional Education Center (PEC), Summer Intensive Program (SIP) and CLEP candidates. Oversee and teach SmartStart technical orientation and online enrollment orientation. Sustains database of test scores on the HU Portal and CampusVue, update necessary spreadsheets, certification rates, announcements, and print certificates Manages inventory of exams and supplies, checks test booklets, supplement book condition at the beginning and end of each test session Responsible for passwords, physical and virtual record security, software updates, training proctors, confidentiality and security of exam questions and student information When required and necessary, notifies University President, Provost, Executive Chief of Staff, Department Chairs, Institutional Effectiveness Manager and faculty of test results as well as any third party or compliance inspection results Additional duties assigned. PROFESSIONAL/PUBLIC ACTIVITIES: Continued education, certifications, and knowledge base enhanced training and skill sets. Attend conference when schedule permits and remain current in the policies, procedures and new business opportunities Must participate in the Hallmark Character Education Program. KNOWLEDGE/ SKILLS/ABILITIES: Ability to pass certification exams for PearsonVue, PSI-Lasergrade, CLEP and ATI Complete training for entrance and placement exam Understand Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) guidelines Computer and systems applications skills Advanced skills in Microsoft Office (particularly in Excel) Excellent oral, presentation, and written communication skills QUALIFICATIONS AND EXPERIENCE: 1. PREFERRED- Bachelor’s Degree from any accredited college/university Experience administering/proctoring standardized exams Experience and certification in proctoring standardized exams 2. REQUIRED- Associate’s Degree from any accredited college/university (prefer IT/Business related), if actively pursuing AAS, requirement may be waived. 1 year of experience working in an educational settin Must pass comprehensive background check to include TSA/FBI background check and must be able to obtain FAA badge for related duties at satellite campus Job Features Job Category Full Time Apply For This Job Full Name * Phone Number * Email * A valid email address is required. Desired Salary * Attach Resume * Submit Copyright © 2026 Hallmark University"
    },
    "https://careers.hallmarkuniversity.edu/jobs/amt-instructor/": {
      "title": "AMT Instructor",
      "description": "AMT Instructor – Careers at Hallmark University Skip to content Main Menu 210.690.9000 Hallmark University Posted 6 months ago AMT Instructor SUMMARY OF THE JOB: Instruct students in all subjects required for AAS Airframe and Powerplant Technology degrees. ESSENTIAL FUNTIONS: • Conduct lectures and demonstrations in assigned subject areas • Lead, supervise, and assist students with practical skill projects • Evaluate student performance of content knowledge and practical skills • Record all grades and submit final course grades to the registrar • Track attendance and submit, daily, to the registrar • All other duties, as assigned OTHER FUNCTIONS: • All full-time faculty are required to participate in the University commencement ceremonies, to include wearing regalia from the college/university of which the degree was received. (Twice Yearly-Spring and Fall, Saturdays) • Partner with the Program Chair for continual course improvement PROFESSIONAL/PUBLIC ACTIVITES: • Mandatory Participation in the Hallmark Character Program: All employees are required to actively engage in this program to embody and promote our core values. KNOWLEDGE/ SKILLS/ABILITIES: • Aviation maintenance of commercial, military, and/or corporate aircraft • Microsoft Office skills: Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook • Strong communication skills including the ability to speak to groups QUALIFICATIONS AND EXPERIENCE: PREFERRED- • Master’s Degree with a concentration in Aviation. • Instructor experience a plus REQUIRED- • FAA Airframe & Powerplant certifications • Bachelor’s degree with a concentration in Aviation, or a commitment to attain • Four years’ experience in aviation maintenance About Hallmark University Hallmark University is a nonprofit university offering degrees in Aviation Maintenance, Information Technology, Cyber Security, Business, and Nursing. Job Features Job Category Full Time Apply For This Job Name * Email * A valid email address is required. Phone * A valid phone number is required. Cover Letter * Attach Resume * Submit Copyright © 2026 Hallmark University"
    },
    "https://careers.hallmarkuniversity.edu/jobs/outbound-call-admissions-specialist/": {
      "title": "Outbound Call Admissions Specialist",
      "description": "Outbound Call Admissions Specialist – Careers at Hallmark University Skip to content Main Menu 210.690.9000 Hallmark University Posted 6 months ago Outbound Call Admissions Specialist SUMMARY OF THE JOB: The Admissions Contact Center Specialist position supports university-wide enrollment efforts for both the on ground and online programs by providing a high volume of recruitment-related call and email support to prospective students. The Admissions Assistant will also be required to display the highest levels of personal integrity and intelligence. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: • Utilize various forms of communication to contact prospective students. • Deliver approved phone script to prospects and in order to better serve interested prospects in their application process, transfer to an Admissions Professional • Identify and overcome objections faced, while keeping the prospects best interest a top priority. • Provide excellent customer service; build excitement and rapport with potential students. • Accurately document all outgoing/incoming prospect activity within Campus Vue CRM (Customer Relationship Management Program) • Make a minimum number of outgoing calls/activities in order to meet or surpass productivity metrics. • Demonstrate desire to succeed within a team environment. OTHER FUNCTIONS: • Display records of achievement in a fast-paced environment • Able to show exceptional social and customer focused skills. • Detail oriented and highly organized. • Display strong ability to effectively interact with staff and faculty. • Proven ability to work in a team environment and confident in interacting with prospective students. • Actively participate in student mentor program. PROFESSIONAL/PUBLIC ACTIVITES: • Mandatory Participation in the Hallmark Character Program: All employees are required to actively engage in this program to embody and promote our core values. KNOWLEDGE/ SKILLS/ABILITIES: • Possess exceptional telephone and face-to-face communication skills. • Exhibit a high level of motivation, with a passion for student success and the Hallmark University mission. • Establish a commitment to business ethics and compliance with regulatory rules. • Ability to multitask and be highly organized in a fast-paced environment, with the ability to adapt to change. • Be proficient in MS Office (Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint, Word, etc.). QUALIFICATIONS AND EXPERIENCE: PREFERRED: • Minimum of an associate degree from an accredited college/university. • Call center & sales experience. REQUIRED: • High School Diploma. • Must have excellent attendance. • Must have excellent customer service skills. • Ability to work afternoons, evenings, and occasional Saturdays. Compensation: $18- $21 About Hallmark University Hallmark University is a nonprofit university offering degrees in Aviation Maintenance, Information Technology, Cyber Security, Business, and Nursing. Job Features Job Category Full Time Apply For This Job Name * Email * A valid email address is required. Phone * A valid phone number is required. Cover Letter * Attach Resume * Submit Copyright © 2026 Hallmark University"
    },
    "https://careers.hallmarkuniversity.edu/jobs/financial-planning-advisor-4/": {
      "title": "Financial Planning Advisor",
      "description": "Financial Planning Advisor – Careers at Hallmark University Skip to content Main Menu 210.690.9000 Staff Hallmark University Posted 1 month ago SUMMARY OF THE JOB: The Financial Planning Advisor assists in carrying out the department’s mission to provide professional knowledge, personalized services and support to students and their families to bridge the gap between family resources and educational expenses.  They develop student financial plans and handle them until they are finalized.  The Financial Planning Advisor needs to make sure that every student is properly funded.  This is made possible by judiciously and respectfully seeking and utilizing all federal, state, and institutional student financial resources available.  They must uphold the highest degree of professionalism, confidentiality, honesty, and integrity when handling student information.  Good communication skills are extremely important, as the position involves daily interaction with students, staff, university personnel, institutional departments, and the community.  Strong basic computer skills are necessary, along with the ability to work without supervision and prioritize the daily duties.  All the laws and regulations related to financial aid must not only be fully understood and applied by the Financial Planning Advisor but also periodically updated.  The Financial Planning Advisor is also responsible for the administration and certification of all Veteran’s benefits. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Learn to interpret and maintain knowledge of complex rules, federal regulations, institutional policies, and procedures pertaining to financial aid. Honor and enforce federal, state and University regulations. Assist with interpretation of above to staff, students, parents, and others. Explain students’ rights and responsibilities for each aid source. Provide financial aid and scholarship information, counseling and advice to prospective students, transfer and reenter students, currently enrolled students, and parents via counseling, telephone, e-mail, and presentations. Assist in providing budgeting, money management, loan indebtedness counseling, entrance and exit loan counseling, to students on an individual and group basis and make presentations to groups during orientation. Develop a tuition plan for all students prior to students starting school. Assist in application process and institutional financial aid applications. Must be capable of making an accurate assessment and evaluation of a person’s financial aid need and award FSA funds based on information gained from applications. Process and maintain financial aid applications and update data as needed using the following software and applications: Ellucian, Colleague, Colleague Self Service, Softdocs, COD, NSLDS, VA Education Platform, HOL Calculator. Proficient knowledge of rules and regulations pertaining to Verification, Professional Judgment and Dependency Override. Must be able to apply this knowledge when advising, packaging and awarding Title IV funds. Responsible for timely collection and completion of required file documents. Audit the documents for accuracy and conflicting data.  Ensure documents and financial aid files are following federal and institutional regulations before approving disbursement of aid to be released. Determine a student’s eligibility for federal student aid taking into consideration the student’s credits, GPA, prior Pell and Loan awards, academic counselor evaluation, and financial need information. Calculate loan eligibility based on COA budget, SAI and other aid received. Authorize and certify student loan amounts. Serves as back-up counselor in the event of other counselors’ absence and assists other departments as needed. Initiate and assist the Business Office in ensuring timely disbursements and refunds of student aid. Initiate and assist the Business Office with in-house and out of school collection accounts. Initiate and assist the Business Office in packaging students for any extra charges. Compare student data with other departments to ensure compliance with federal regulations and institutional policy and procedures. (Admissions, Registrar, Loan Default Management, Business Office, and Education Department.) Advise students regarding Satisfactory Academic Progress, Withdrawals and Leave of Absence. Mentor students and maintain client relations. Serve as a liaison between students/parents and lenders/loan service providers. Meet schedules and budgets assigned by the Director of Financial Planning. Must be proficient in all aspects of Veterans Benefits. OTHER FUNCTIONS: Review status change forms received from the Registrar Office daily. Adjust financial aid awards accordingly.  Initiate third party notification requirements. EX: VA, WIA, Direct Loan Servicing Center, NSLDS, UNISA Check Title IV Credit Balances by term. Every term check potential graduate account balance and conduct a final file audit. Verify Exit Counseling has been completed. At the start of every term electronically certify individual students VA Enrollment Certification using VA Education Platform. Maintain, compare, and audit VA certification from previous terms. Set up refunds and adjust in Colleague UI. Set up/adjust payment plans, refunds, and stipends for students daily. Daily review of Transfer-in Credit Forms received from the Registrar office and adjust all prior and future financial aid awards. Update award information in Colleague UI. Notify and counsel students accordingly. Receive payments and write receipts in the absence of student accounts for in school payments, registration fees, or caps/gowns. Assist with Transcript distribution/evaluation if Registrar is not available. Provide verification to third parties at student request for cost breakdown of tuition/fees, credits earned, and length of program. For Tuition Assistance, WIA, Insurance, apartment/housing, SNAP, and any other agency. Repackage students every term for Academic Year 2 – 5 Monthly Enrollment Certification on NSLDS (600+ students) f/k/a SSCR. Add new students to the Transfer Monitoring List on NSLDS at the start of every term. Attend and serve as Hallmark representative at local, state, regional/national conferences and training seminars concerning student financial aid and student services. Actively participate in Student Mentor and Hallmark Character program. PROFESSIONAL/PUBLIC ACTIVITIES: Participate in activities aimed at professional development beyond the university in-service requirements. Regularly attend state and regional seminars, conferences and self-training providing current information about the delivery of financial aid services. Mandatory Participation in the Hallmark Character Program: All employees are required to actively engage in this program to embody and promote our core values. KNOWLEDGE/ SKILLS/ABILITIES: Ability to work in a fast-paced environment. A variety of students and issues may present themselves, so the Financial Planning Advisor must possess the ability to respond effectively and to work on several tasks at the same time. Ability to be proactive, innovative and solutions oriented. Good working knowledge of student aid programs, related regulations and federal need analysis system required. Good analytical and math skills required. Ability to apply concepts such as fractions, percentages, ratios, and proportions to practical situations. Position requires sitting for an extended period at a desk and computer. Commitment to a student-centered learning environment and student success. Team builder with excellent interpersonal skills and ability to work effectively with faculty, staff, and students. Outstanding oral, written, interpersonal and presentation communication skills. Effective computer skills. QUALIFICATIONS AND EXPERIENCE: REQUIRED High School Diploma/GED and some college/university credits. PREFERRED Minimum one year experience awarding student financial aid and working in a Financial Aid Office in a technical school, college, or university. Strong working knowledge of student aid programs, related regulations and federal need analysis system required. Strong analytical and math skills required. Ability to apply concepts such as fractions, percentages, ratios, and proportions to practical situations. Position requires sitting for an extended period at a desk and computer. Ability to multitask and work independently. Compensation: $43,000–$50,000 per year, based on experience and qualifications. Job Features Job Category Full Time Apply For This Job Name * Email * A valid email address is required. Phone * United States +1 United Kingdom +44 Afghanistan (‫افغانستان‬‎) +93 Albania (Shqipëri) +355 Algeria (‫الجزائر‬‎) +213 American Samoa +1 Andorra +376 Angola +244 Anguilla +1 Antigua and Barbuda +1 Argentina +54 Armenia (Հայաստան) +374 Aruba +297 Australia +61 Austria (Österreich) +43 Azerbaijan (Azərbaycan) +994 Bahamas +1 Bahrain (‫البحرين‬‎) +973 Bangladesh (বাংলাদেশ) +880 Barbados +1 Belarus (Беларусь) +375 Belgium (België) +32 Belize +501 Benin (Bénin) +229 Bermuda +1 Bhutan (འབྲུག) +975 Bolivia +591 Bosnia and Herzegovina (Босна и Херцеговина) +387 Botswana +267 Brazil (Brasil) +55 British Indian Ocean Territory +246 British Virgin Islands +1 Brunei +673 Bulgaria (България) +359 Burkina Faso +226 Burundi (Uburundi) +257 Cambodia (កម្ពុជា) +855 Cameroon (Cameroun) +237 Canada +1 Cape Verde (Kabu Verdi) +238 Caribbean Netherlands +599 Cayman Islands +1 Central African Republic (République centrafricaine) +236 Chad (Tchad) +235 Chile +56 China (中国) +86 Christmas Island +61 Cocos (Keeling) Islands +61 Colombia +57 Comoros (‫جزر القمر‬‎) +269 Congo (DRC) (Jamhuri ya Kidemokrasia ya Kongo) +243 Congo (Republic) (Congo-Brazzaville) +242 Cook Islands +682 Costa Rica +506 Côte d’Ivoire +225 Croatia (Hrvatska) +385 Cuba +53 Curaçao +599 Cyprus (Κύπρος) +357 Czech Republic (Česká republika) +420 Denmark (Danmark) +45 Djibouti +253 Domini