    "https://careers.hallmarkuniversity.edu/jobs/director-of-marketing-2/": {
      "title": "Director of Marketing",
      "description": "Director of Marketing – Careers at Hallmark University Skip to content Main Menu 210.690.9000 Staff Hallmark University Posted 1 month ago Position Summary: Hallmark University is seeking a forward-thinking Director of Marketing to lead an integrated marketing function focused on enrollment growth, brand strength, and institutional visibility. This leader owns the strategy that generates qualified student interest, strengthens the University’s reputation, and connects prospective students, families, employers, and the community with Hallmark’s mission of developing superior skills, knowledge, and character. Essential Responsibilities: Develop and execute a multiyear marketing and communications strategy aligned with university growth, enrollment priorities, program capacity, and brand objectives. Translate enrollment goals into annual and term-based campaign plans, channel strategies, budgets, forecasts, and measurable performance targets. Own enrollment demand generation and the inquiry portfolio, balancing lead volume, quality, cost, conversion, and program-specific demand. Use Salesforce to govern campaign attribution, lead sources, segmentation, funnel reporting, dashboards, integrations, and data quality. Direct SEM and paid-search strategy across Google and Microsoft/Bing, including keywords, bidding, landing pages, creative testing, and optimization. Lead paid social and video across Facebook/Meta, Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, LinkedIn, streaming/CTV, display, and retargeting. Evaluate emerging platforms, changing audience behavior, automation, personalization, and responsible AI tools that can increase brand awareness and student interest. Own marketing oversight of the University website, including content strategy, user experience, SEO, landing pages, conversion paths, accessibility, analytics, and ongoing optimization. Oversee organic social media, content planning, public storytelling, reputation management, and coordinated public-relations activity. Lead the in-house creative function across design, video, photography, copywriting, campaign concepts, advertising, collateral, and institutional communications. Serve as the University’s brand steward, maintaining visual identity, messaging, voice, positioning, and internal brand governance across colleges and departments. Own media placement strategy, procurement, vendor and agency performance, project management, and allocation of marketing resources. Establish a performance cadence using cost per inquiry, cost per application and start, conversion, channel efficiency, website performance, attribution completeness, and return on marketing investment. Lead and develop the marketing team while partnering with Admissions, Academic Affairs, Advancement, Student Affairs, Career Services, IT, and senior leadership. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Strategic leadership across integrated campaigns, enrollment marketing, brand management, and measurable growth. Hands-on fluency with SEM/PPC, paid social, streaming media, SEO, web analytics, conversion optimization, and media planning. Ability to translate Salesforce and marketing data into clear priorities, budget decisions, and corrective action. Strong creative judgment and experience directing advertising, video, design, content, and brand communications. Working knowledge of website concepts, HTML/CSS, tagging, digital accessibility, and quality assurance. Sound vendor, budget, project, account-security, privacy, and advertising-compliance management. Curiosity about emerging platforms and disciplined experimentation with AI-assisted creative, analytics, and automation. Professional/Public Activities: Mandatory participation in the Hallmark Character Program and active support of the University’s mission, values, and professional standards. Continued education, certifications, and ongoing development of current marketing knowledge and leadership skills. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications, business, digital media, or a related field. Eight or more years of progressive marketing experience leading integrated campaigns, digital acquisition, brand management, and measurable growth. Four or more years of leadership experience managing teams, agencies, major portfolios, or cross-functional programs. Demonstrated expertise in SEM/PPC, paid social, SEO, web analytics, conversion optimization, media placement, and campaign measurement. Experience using Salesforce or a comparable CRM for campaign attribution, lead-source management, reporting, and funnel analysis. Demonstrated ability to manage significant budgets, prioritize competing investments, and turn data into decisive action. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in marketing, communications, business, or a related discipline. Experience marketing higher education, workforce education, or another complex lead-generation portfolio. Working knowledge of Adobe Creative Cloud, marketing automation, tag management, business intelligence, and AI-assisted workflows. Benefits: Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision insurance 401(k) retirement plan Paid time off Professional development and opportunities for growth and advancement Job Features Job Category Full Time Apply For This Job Name * Email * A valid email address is required. Phone * A valid phone number is required. Cover Letter * Attach Resume * Submit Copyright © 2026 Hallmark University"
    },
    "https://careers.hallmarkuniversity.edu/jobs/3323/": {
      "title": "Financial Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Financial Services Coordinator – Careers at Hallmark University Skip to content Main Menu 210.690.9000 Staff Hallmark University Posted 3 weeks ago Position Summary Monitors both in-school and out-of-school accounts receivable, counsels’ students that are past due, perform collection activities, and posts payments to accounts. Responsible for the coordination and execution of all purchasing activities across the organization. Responsibilities will include but not be limited to, securing contracts/services with current and potential vendors, negotiation, review, and approval of contract/service terms and conditions, obtaining competitive pricing for projects and recurring purchases, and any supplier management conditions that may affect the organization. Essential Responsibilities Cash Receipts/Posting Payments • Enter cash payments (cash, check/money order, credit card) to the student’s ledger card • Create a daily batch sheet to include all payments received • Reconcile GP postings Collections • Contacting permanent-out delinquent accounts by telephone and written communication • Contacting active students by telephone and/or pulling them from class to maintain adequate monthly collections • Recommend lockouts for delinquent accounts • Send delinquent permanent-out accounts to collection service Additional Duties • Monitor credit balances on student ledgers; report to financial planning for refunding via • check/ACH • Provide administrative support for Financial Affairs Purchasing • Direct and manage the purchasing activities of the university; to include but not be limited to, review of planned orders, create requisitions for purchased items, confirm system lead times, delivery dates and costs, inspection of merchandise or products to determine quality/value, and authorize payment of invoices and return of merchandise. • Receiving, processing, documenting and executing purchases and procurements according to Hallmark University policies and procedures. Ensure compliance with federal, state and local laws and regulations; maintain necessary documentation for proper invoicing and billing. • Book inventory management – process book/tool orders, maintain safety stock, calculate monthly inventory, process returns and credits, negotiate annual forward buys, update ISBN revisions and price lists, and maintain all onsite and virtual inventories. • Provide accurate and timely supplier negotiations and contracts based on defined category criteria (i.e. cost, quality, productivity, service). • Analyzes, evaluates, and identifies preferred vendors based on specific performance criteria. • Reviews, updates, and maintains purchase orders until they are closed. • Participate in the on-going development of efficient processes for an effective purchasing system. • All other duties, as assigned Knowledge/Skills/ Abilities • Ability to communicate professionally and effectively • Ability to interact with all levels staff & management • Procurement • Project Management • Contract Management • Billing Procedures • Detail oriented & problem solver with ability to multitask • Excellent research skills • Proficiency in MS Office, especially MS Excel Required Qualification: • 5+ years’ experience in business/office environment • High School Diploma or GED Preferred Qualifications • Associates degree, preferably in accounting or related business field from an accredited university or college • Working knowledge of Fair Debt Collection Practices Act & FERPA • Familiarity with student loans and financial aid Professional/Public Activities: • Continuing professional development • Attend informational webinars and potential conferences. • Mandatory Participation in the Hallmark Character Program: All employees are required to actively engage in this program to embody and promote our core values. Job Features Job Category Full Time Apply For This Job Name * Email * A valid email address is required. Phone * A valid phone number is required. Cover Letter * Attach Resume * Submit Copyright © 2026 Hallmark University"
    },
    "https://careers.hallmarkuniversity.edu/jobs/dean-school-of-technology/": {
      "title": "Dean, School of Technology",
      "description": "Dean, School of Technology – Careers at Hallmark University Skip to content Main Menu 210.690.9000 Staff Hallmark University Posted 3 weeks ago Position summary The Dean provides academic and administrative leadership for the School of Technology, advancing Hallmark University’s mission to change individual lives through superior skills, knowledge, and character. The Dean leads faculty, curriculum, student learning, continuous improvement, employer engagement, and responsible use of school resources in an accelerated, career-focused educational environment. The position oversees four programs: Bachelor of Science in Artificial Intelligence, Bachelor of Science in Cybersecurity, Bachelor of Science in Information Systems, and Master of Science in Cybersecurity. The Dean translates industry needs and institutional priorities into rigorous instruction, applied learning, relevant certifications, and measurable student success. Academic and program leadership · Develop and execute the school’s annual academic and operational plan with the Vice President of Academic Affairs. Align priorities, staffing, course schedules, and resource requests with approved institutional goals and program demand. · Lead regular curriculum review with faculty, instructional design, and industry advisors. Maintain clear program outcomes, course sequencing, prerequisites, current syllabi, and applied assessments across in-person, hybrid, and online delivery. BS in Artificial Intelligence: Guide a coherent progression through computing, programming, mathematics, data preparation, machine learning, and applied AI. Ensure students evaluate model performance, limitations, privacy, security, bias, and responsible use through practical projects. BS in Cybersecurity: Maintain applied coverage of secure systems and networks, threat analysis, security operations, incident response, risk management, and ethical practice. Align learning activities with relevant workforce competencies and certification objectives. BS in Information Systems: Connect systems analysis, databases, enterprise applications, infrastructure, and project management to organizational needs. Emphasize requirements gathering, solution implementation, data-informed decisions, and communication with business stakeholders. MS in Cybersecurity: Maintain advanced expectations for security architecture, risk and governance, analytical inquiry, and a culminating applied experience. Coordinate with the designated graduate education supervisor and qualified program manager to sustain graduate rigor and faculty qualifications. Essential responsibilities Faculty leadership and instructional quality: Recruit, recommend selection of, orient, mentor, and evaluate faculty in coordination with Academic Affairs and Human Resources. Verify qualifications for assigned courses; schedule prepared faculty before each term; manage workloads and instructional continuity; and support current technical and teaching expertise. · Observe teaching and review courses across delivery formats. Use student learning evidence, course reviews, and feedback to guide faculty development and documented improvement. Support accessible course design, timely feedback, and meaningful instructor engagement. Student learning and success: Work with faculty, Student Affairs, the Registrar, and Career Services to identify academic barriers, implement early interventions, and improve progression, retention, completion, and career readiness. Address student academic concerns and appeals within university policy and delegated authority. · Integrate Hallmark’s Character Program, professional communication, teamwork, ethical judgment, and accountability into instruction and applied projects. Maintain academic integrity and clear expectations for responsible student and faculty use of AI. Assessment and accreditation: Lead program learning-outcome assessment and annual program review. Maintain evidence of findings, improvement actions, and subsequent results. Prepare school reports and accreditation materials with Institutional Effectiveness and Compliance, and support approved program changes through university processes. · Maintain documented arrangements for doctoral supervision of graduate education, qualified management of the MS in Cybersecurity, and course-specific faculty credentialing. The Dean fulfills these additional roles only when individually qualified and formally designated. Industry relationships and applied learning: Lead Program Advisory Committee activities with appropriate representation for each program and degree level. Document employer feedback, recommendations, decisions, and follow-through. Maintain productive relationships with technology employers and academic partners. · Partner with Career Services and employers to develop internships, applied projects, employer presentations, mentoring, and hiring opportunities. Support Hallmark Consulting Group projects where appropriate, with defined learning outcomes, faculty supervision, and client expectations. · Oversee relevant certification pathways, preparation, exam access, and results. Use certification evidence alongside broader learning assessments to improve instruction and graduate readiness. Operations and stewardship: Prepare and manage the approved school budget. Plan faculty capacity, instructional labs, software, cloud and AI computing resources, and equipment replacement. Coordinate with university IT on secure, reliable learning environments, appropriate access, and protection of student and project data. · Collaborate with Admissions and Marketing on accurate program information and prospective-student engagement. Evaluate proposed program enhancements against employer demand, learning quality, staffing capacity, and financial sustainability. · Provide term-based performance updates and an annual report of accomplishments, priorities, and corrective actions. Participate in university committees, relevant professional activities, and other duties consistent with the position. Required qualifications · An earned master’s degree in a related field, such as information technology, cybersecurity, information systems, computer science, artificial intelligence, data science, or a closely related discipline, from an appropriately accredited institution or recognized international equivalent. · At least four years of related practical professional experience in one or more technology disciplines represented by the school, with evidence of current technical knowledge and applied problem-solving. · At least three years of progressive leadership experience with responsibility for people, programs, projects, or budgets. Relevant roles may include department chair, program director, dean, technology manager, or comparable leadership positions. Leadership and professional experience may overlap. · Demonstrated higher education teaching, curriculum development, or academic program leadership experience, including assessment of student learning and improvement of instruction. · Experience supervising or developing faculty or professional staff, managing competing priorities, and working effectively with students, colleagues, and external partners. · Ability to lead across AI, cybersecurity, and information systems while drawing on faculty expertise; interpret performance data; manage resources; and communicate technical and academic matters clearly. · Commitment to Hallmark University’s mission, purpose, character development, academic integrity, student success, and respectful treatment of others. Preferred qualifications · An earned PhD or other doctorate in a related technology discipline, or in education or leadership with substantial relevant technical graduate preparation and professional experience. · Experience leading undergraduate and graduate technology programs, supporting accreditation and institutional effectiveness, and managing accelerated, hybrid, or online instruction. · Evidence of improving student learning, retention, completion, certification attainment, or employment outcomes through documented academic initiatives. · Current industry certification appropriate to the candidate’s expertise, such as CISSP, CISM, or a relevant cloud, networking, data, or AI credential; experience developing employer partnerships and applied learning opportunities. Teaching and graduate leadership assignments Any teaching assignment requires separate review and documented approval of qualifications for the specific course and degree level under university policy and applicable accreditation requirements. Appointment as Dean does not automatically authorize graduate teaching or designation as the institution’s graduate education supervisor. Teaching assignments are established by the Vice President of Academic Affairs in light of school leadership responsibilities. Schedule and performance expectations Maintain an accessible campus presence and availability for students and faculty across delivery formats. Occasional evening and Saturday responsibilities and local employer or university events are required as scheduled. Performance is evaluated against agreed goals for learning quality, student success, faculty effectiveness, employer engagement, operational readiness, and budget stewardship, with shared responsibilities recognized. Job Features Job Category Full Time Apply For This Job Name * Email * A valid email address is required. Phone * United States +1 United Kingdom +44 Afghanistan (‫افغانستان‬‎) +93 Albania (Shqipëri) +355 Algeria (‫الجزائر‬‎) +213 American Samoa +1 Andorra +376 Angola +244 Anguilla +1 Antigua and Barbuda +1 Argentina +54 Armenia (Հայաստան) +374 Aruba +297 Australia +61 Austria (Österreich) +43 Azerbaijan (Azərbaycan) +994 Bahamas +1 Bahrain (‫البحرين‬‎) +973 Bangladesh (বাংলাদেশ) +880 Barbados +1 Belarus (Беларусь) +375 Belgium (België) +32 Belize +501 Benin (Bénin) +229 Bermuda +1 Bhutan (འབྲུག) +975 Bolivi